  "body": "## What changed\n\nA planned corner relief whose start no pass vertex reaches, and for which no legal detour exists, was dropped without a diagnostic (#3249). It could leave material the operator does not expect.\n\n- `inject_relief_spurs` (`crates/motion/src/machining2d/corner_relief_spur.rs`) now reports each skipped relief: the caller gets the relief start points in a `misses` vector.\n- The pocket emit path (`pocket_emit.rs`) and the pocket avoid path (`pocket_avoid.rs`) write one note per corner into the `PathBuilder` / path notes: `corner relief at (x, y) is not cut: no pass vertex reaches the relief spur`. Notes are de-duplicated by corner, so a multi-level cut or a retry names each corner once.\n- The four-dogbones rest test keeps its no-note assert: a reached relief adds no note.\n\nChangelog: A 2D Pocket corner relief that no pass reaches is now named in the operation notes instead of being dropped silently.\n\n## Pinning tests\n\n- `machining2d::corner_relief_spur::tests::a_relief_no_pass_reaches_is_reported_as_a_miss` (crates/motion/src/machining2d/corner_relief_spur.rs): the miss is reported and no spur is spliced in; a reached relief reports no miss and gets its spur.\n- `unreachable_corners_and_bad_overrides_are_refused` (crates/motion/tests/corner_relief.rs): the island-blocked spur refuses at plan time.\n- `crates/motion/tests/rest_corner_relief.rs`: the rest pass keeps its no-note assert.\n\n## Not exercised\n\n- The note text in a posted NC program through the full post pipeline.\n- The avoid-path note on a multi-level cut with more than one skipped corner.\n\nFork synced at v0.25.0\n\nFixes #3249\n",
